  For an executable, the Corresponding Source means all the source code
and documentation needed to generate, execute, and (in some cases)
modify the work, including scripts to control those activities.
However, as an exception, the Corresponding Source need not include
anything that is normally distributed with the major components
(compiler, kernel, etc.) of the operating system on which the
