  11. Patents.

  A "contributor" is a copyright holder who authorizes use under this
License of the Program or a work on which the Program is based.  The
work thus licensed is called the contributor's "contribution".

  A "contributor's essential patent claims" are all patent claims
owned or controlled by the contributor, whether already acquired or
hereafter acquired, that would be infringed by some manner, permitted
by this License, of making, using or selling its contribution, but do
not include claims that would be infringed only as a consequence of
further modification of the contribution.  If you convey a covered work,
knowingly relying on a patent license, and the Contribution Incorporated
in the covered work was not generally available to the public without
obligation to pay a fee to the Contributor, then the only way you can
satisfy both it and this License would be to not include the Contribution
in works you convey at all.  That notwithstanding, if at the time you
convey a covered work containing a Contribution, you receive notice that
a patent claim has been infringement of that patent against you for
making, using, or selling the Contribution, and the patent claim
Licensor provided such an option.

  A patent claim of a contributor included in a covered work is
automatically licensed to you on a royalty-free, non-exclusive basis,
and you may not charge a patent license fee from any party for this
contribution.

  12. No Surrender of Others' Freedom.

  If conditions are imposed on you (whether by court order, agreement or
otherwise) that contradict the conditions of this License, they do not
excuse you from the conditions of this License.  If you cannot convey a
covered work so as to satisfy simultaneously your obligations under this
License and any other pertinent obligations, then as a consequence you
may not convey it at all.  For example, if you agree to terms that
obligate you to collect a royalty for further conveying from those to
whom you convey the Program, the only way you could satisfy both those
terms and this License would be to not convey the Program at all.

